{#
  PersistentVolumeClaim for a k8s-hosted service — the plain RWO/longhorn-family body that
  authelia, crowdsec, loki-homelab, mosquitto, pihole (both claims), registry, valheim-stats and
  wg-easy share. Each carries its own WHY for the storage class / backup posture it picked,
  which stays at the call site (via `{% call %}`) rather than being swallowed here — the whole
  point of these comments is that they differ role to role.

  THE CALLER SLOT SITS BETWEEN `spec:` AND `accessModes:`, and that is what decides whether a
  role can adopt this at all. pi-peer-backup and valheim are deliberately NOT converted: each
  attaches a load-bearing comment to `storageClassName` — "Plain `longhorn` ON PURPOSE (not
  -nobackup)" and "nobackup: every byte here is re-downloadable from Steam" — and this macro
  can only place a comment above `accessModes:`. Converting them would move the reasoning off
  the line that makes the trade-off, which is the one place it is worth having.

  freshrss and zigbee2mqtt are excluded for the same reason as code-server below, and were
  checked rather than assumed: each declares a claim in `k8s_autodeploy_snapshot_pvcs`
  (freshrss-config, zigbee2mqtt-data) AND renders that claim in its own template, so each is a
  role the textual guard actually checks. Converting either would leave it checking nothing.

  code-server's pvc-workspace.yaml.j2 has the identical body but is deliberately NOT converted:
  ansible/tests/deploy/_autodeploy.py's `_rendered_pvc_claims` (consumed by
  test_k8s_autodeploy_guard.py::test_snapshot_pvc_declarations_match_rendered_claims) greps a
  role's own `templates/*.j2` text for a literal `kind: PersistentVolumeClaim` block — it does
  not render Jinja, so a claim built via this macro is invisible to it. code-server is the only
  one of the five whose `k8s_autodeploy_snapshot_pvcs` declares that specific claim name, so it
  is the only one the guard actually checks; the other four have no such declaration and the gap
  is inert for them. See "Textual guard checks break on an indirection" in project memory.

  Arguments:
    name           PVC name; matches whatever claimName a Deployment mounts.
    storage_class  e.g. `longhorn`, `longhorn-nobackup`, or a role's own `*_k8s_storage_class`.
    size           e.g. a role's own `*_k8s_storage` / `*_k8s_size` default.

  Call with a body to insert a comment block between `spec:` and `accessModes:`; call plain
  (no `{% call %}`) when there's nothing to say there.
#}
{% macro pvc(name, storage_class, size) -%}
apiVersion: v1
kind: PersistentVolumeClaim
metadata:
  name: {{ name }}
  namespace: {{ k8s_namespace }}
spec:
{% if caller is defined %}{{ caller() }}{% endif %}
  accessModes:
    - ReadWriteOnce
  storageClassName: {{ storage_class }}
  resources:
    requests:
      storage: {{ size }}
{% endmacro %}
